\chapter{The Stay A While queue API}

Stay A While is the EECS queueing system.
We want to access its documented REST API both from Python and from the
shell.

We therefore provide two interfaces:
first, a class, [[StayawhileSession]], that wraps the HTTP API;
second, a Typer CLI rooted at [[kthutils stayawhile]].

The server (the [[queue-dev]] repository on KTH GitHub, a Rust/Rocket
application) exposes one route family per concern, and each route is
protected by one of two guards:
[[Auth]] accepts only the browser JWT, while [[ApiAuth]] accepts the JWT
\emph{or} a long-lived API key.
\Cref{tab:stayawhile-routes} is the map we keep in sync with the server;
the rest of this chapter walks through it family by family, and the CLI
mirrors the same grouping.
