\section{Caller identity}

[[/api/user]] identifies the current caller and uses the browser-backed
session token---the same [[Auth]] guard as the API-key management endpoints.
The reply is the very object the web client keeps in its [[userdata]]
cookie, so besides [[username]], [[realname]] and [[provider_id]] it carries
the role lists [[teacher_in]] and [[assistant_in]] and---importantly---the
caller's JWT in [[token]].
The session returns it unchanged; the CLI picks the fields it shows, so the
token never ends up in a terminal log by accident.
