\subsection{Locking and messages}

Queue locking lets a teacher prevent new students from joining while still
serving those already in line.
Unlocking also clears all TA check-ins, so assistants must re-check-in for
the new session---a useful side-effect when transitioning between lab
groups.
The lock endpoint uses [[POST]] to lock and [[DELETE]] to unlock; both are
recorded as [[close]]/[[open]] events in the queue-event log
(\cref{sec:stayawhile-logs}).

The two messages a queue carries are set with [[PUT]] and a
[[{"message": "..."}]] body.
The MOTD is shown prominently at the top of the queue page and the queue
info (\enquote{köinfo}) in the sidebar.
An empty string clears either message; there is no separate delete
endpoint, which is why [[set_motd(queue, "")]] is the way to clear.
<<[[StayawhileSession]] methods>>=
def lock_queue(self, queue):
  """Lock `queue` so new users cannot join it."""
  return self._request("POST",
                       self._queue_path(queue, "lock"),
                       use_api_key=True)


def unlock_queue(self, queue):
  """Unlock `queue` so new users can join it.

  Also clears all TA check-ins for the queue.
  """
  return self._request("DELETE",
                       self._queue_path(queue, "lock"),
                       use_api_key=True)


def set_motd(self, queue, message):
  """Set the message of the day for `queue`; empty string clears it."""
  return self._request("PUT",
                       self._queue_path(queue, "motd"),
                       payload={"message": message},
                       use_api_key=True)


def set_info(self, queue, message):
  """Set the queue info text for `queue`; empty string clears it."""
  return self._request("PUT",
                       self._queue_path(queue, "info"),
                       payload={"message": message},
                       use_api_key=True)
