\section{Queue statistics}

All statistics endpoints are teacher-only and share one queue path prefix.
They split into two kinds.
The range queries---[[sessions]], [[assistants]] and
[[interaction_sessions]]---take optional [[from]] and [[until]] dates
(YYYY-MM-DD, interpreted in Stockholm time) and default to the last
90~days; the server rejects [[until]] without [[from]].
The date-addressed queries give the detail and the hourly breakdown of one
day's sessions and put the date in the path, under an explicit [[date/]]
segment.
That segment is not decoration: the server also serves
[[statistics/sessions/<session_key>]] for a numeric session id, so a bare
date in that position fails to parse as an integer and yields a~404.
The range parameters come from [[date_range_params]]
(\cref{sec:stayawhile-presence}).
