\section{Bookings}

Teachers can list, upload, and clear bookings for a queue, while any user can
inspect their own booking for one queue.
The upload body is a JSON array of objects with [[provider_id]],
[[slot_time]] and an optional [[entry_type]] ([[help]] or [[present]],
defaulting to [[present]]).
[[provider_id]] is the identity the login provider issues (a [[u1...]]
KTH~id), but the server also resolves a plain username, first against its
own user table and then against LDAP, so a teacher can upload straight from
a class list.
The field used to be called [[ugkthid]]; the server still accepts that name
as a deserialisation alias, but it is on its way out, so we only ever emit
[[provider_id]].

The upload is an upsert keyed on queue, student and slot time, and it is
partial by design: identifiers that cannot be resolved are reported in
[[skipped]] (with [[error]] set to [[unresolved_identifiers]]) while the
rest are stored and returned in [[bookings]].
We pass that reply through so the caller can decide what to do about the
skipped ones.
The listing returns the stored bookings joined with the user table---
[[username]], [[realname]], [[provider_id]], [[slot_time]], a boolean
[[help]] and [[uploaded_at]]---so it is the booking \emph{view}, not the
upload format, that comes back.

Clearing all bookings is rarely intended---a teacher usually wants to remove
one day's bookings (for instance, after cancelling a lab session) without
affecting future dates.
The clear endpoint therefore accepts optional [[from]] and [[until]] date
parameters (YYYY-MM-DD, Stockholm time) that restrict deletion to a date
range, and it never deletes past bookings.
It reports how many bookings it removed as [[{"deleted": n}]], which we
pass through unchanged.
<<[[StayawhileSession]] methods>>=
def list_bookings(self, queue):
  """Return the bookings for `queue`."""
  return self._request("GET",
                       self._queue_path(queue, "bookings"),
                       use_api_key=True)


def upsert_bookings(self, queue, bookings):
  """Upload or update `bookings` for `queue`; returns bookings and skipped."""
  return self._request("POST",
                       self._queue_path(queue, "bookings"),
                       payload=bookings,
                       use_api_key=True)


def clear_bookings(self, queue, from_date=None, until=None):
  """Delete future bookings for `queue`, optionally in a date range."""
  return self._request("DELETE",
                       self._queue_path(queue, "bookings"),
                       params=date_range_params(from_date, until),
                       use_api_key=True)
