\section{Logs and help history}
\label{sec:stayawhile-logs}

The API provides three teacher-facing logs and one student-facing
help-history endpoint.
All three logs take the same optional [[from]]/[[until]] range (YYYY-MM-DD,
default the last 90~days), and the interaction log additionally filters on
[[type]].
They record different things, and it is the difference that tells a
maintainer which one to reach for:
\begin{description}
\item[Queue log] one entry per join or leave event, with the queue size at
  that moment: [[username]], [[realname]], [[time]], [[help]],
  [[left_queue]], [[queue_length]], [[help_amount]], [[present_amount]] and
  the student's [[comment]].
\item[Interaction log] one entry per help or presentation session:
  [[helper_username]], [[helper_name]], [[student_username]],
  [[student_name]], [[started_at]], [[ended_at]] ([[null]] while ongoing),
  [[duration_secs]] and [[help]].
\item[Queue events] one entry per open or close of the queue:
  [[event_type]] ([[open]] or [[close]]) and [[occurred_at]].
  The statistics use these to delimit lab sessions.
\end{description}
None of the logs carries a [[provider_id]]; the usernames are the stable
join key between them.
<<[[StayawhileSession]] methods>>=
